extends RefCounted
## Ship kit: turns a build (part id -> count, as in Game.build) into placed sprites.
## The builder screen draws the craft through this file only; it never positions parts itself.
##
## PUBLIC API (keep these signatures; the builder depends on them):
##   ShipKit.layout(build)            -> Array of placed items, back to front
##   ShipKit.next_slot(build, id)     -> where one more `id` would attach
##   ShipKit.bounds(build)            -> Rect2 around the whole craft
##   ShipKit.draw(ci, origin, build)  -> draw the craft
##   ShipKit.icon(id)                 -> Texture2D for the parts bin (fits in 24x24), or null
##   ShipKit.launcher(rocket_id)      -> Texture2D of the launch vehicle (bottom-centre anchored), or null
##   ShipKit.launcher_icon(rocket_id) -> Texture2D for the parts bin (fits in 24x24), or null
##
## Coordinates are in pixels relative to the ship ORIGIN = the centre of the spacecraft bus.
## +x is right, +y is down. Everything sits on whole pixels.
##
## A placed item is a Dictionary:
##   "id":   String   part id from Data.PARTS, or a decoration ("engine", "yoke", "rail", "heatshield_front")
##   "n":    int      index among the items of the same id (0 for the first)
##   "tex":  Texture2D or null (null = draw `rect` as a flat box in `color`)
##   "pos":  Vector2  top-left corner of the sprite
##   "flip": bool     draw mirrored left-right
##   "rect": Rect2    hit area for picking the part off the ship (zero size for decorations: never hit)
##   "color": Color   only for boxes without a texture
##   extra fields:  "box": Rect2 the whole sprite;  "deco": true on decorations;  "owner": the part a
##                  decoration belongs to (it lights up with it)
## To pick a part under the mouse walk the array from the END (front) and take the first item whose
## rect has the point.
##
## next_slot returns {} when the part is at its maximum, else a Dictionary:
##   "node": Vector2  the attach point to light up (green dot)
##   "rect": Rect2    where the new sprite will sit
##   "pos":  Vector2  its top-left corner      "tex": Texture2D or null      "flip": bool
##
## HOW THE CRAFT GROWS
##   deck (top):   ascent stage in the middle (the dish then stands on its docking port), high-gain dish,
##                 medium-gain dish left, parachute can right, low-gain mast in front
##   walls:        solar panels alternate right / left, 4 per wing, panels 9-16 form a second wing behind;
##                 RTGs alternate right / left on a boom chain; Ka dish boom right, magnetometer boom left
##   faces:        batteries and recorders fill the two racks, camera, spectrometer, dust analyzer, drill
##   below:        propellant: units 1-24 fill three stacked core tanks (3 px of barrel per unit), units
##                 25-80 fill two radial tanks with their own engines, right and left in turn ("prop"
##                 items: n 0-2 = core tanks from the top, 3 = right tank, 4 = left tank);
##                 legs, airbags and the heat shield move down as the stack grows; rovers and the drone
##                 hang from a rail under the bus and move outward when a radial tank is in the way
##   sunshade:     curved cloth panel on standoffs left of the bus (the Sun side), behind everything else
##   hull:         pressure bowl round the lower bus: "hull" (whole bowl) sits behind the tanks and the gear,
##                 its part above the bus bottom ("hull_front", a decoration that can be picked) covers the
##                 lower bus; batteries, recorders and instruments still mount on top of it

